<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greek War of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1830">1830</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Greek War of Independence was a revolt by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> against Ottoman rule in the 1820s, which ended with international recognition of an independent Greek state in 1830. European powers intervened decisively on the Greek side. For the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> it was an early instance of a nationalist movement detaching territory, part of the pattern of its gradual decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greek-war-of-independence.jpg" alt="Greek War of Independence" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SJCAmerican · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greek_revolution_collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
